  "id": "COMPOUND:26395 - PROTEIN:3990",
  "verbalization": "Excisusin B is implicated in the relationship with the Inner centromere protein through multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that Excisusin B acts as a target for several compounds, including Werner syndrome ATP-dependent helicase, 19-Oxo-3-beta,5,14-trihydroxy-5-beta-bufa-20,22-dienolide-3-acetate, and multidrug resistance-associated protein 7. These compounds, in turn, are targets of other molecules that ultimately lead to the Inner centromere protein. The scores from the different paths indicate a consistent pattern of interaction, with Excisusin B being a central node in the network of targets leading to the Inner centromere protein. The mechanisms involved appear to be related to cellular processes involving DNA repair and chromosomal stability, as suggested by the involvement of the Werner syndrome ATP-dependent helicase. The evidence supports a potential role for Excisusin B in modulating these processes, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
